nd logs like “failed to setup informer”/remote watch errors; **Mitigation:** constrain discovery scope, add backpressure/rate limiting around informer setup, and shard by environment (separate controller instances) if you need to scale beyond a single leader.\n- **Failure mode:** Remote-cluster discovery partially or permanently missing; **Trigger:** workload identity misconfig or missing GKE location fields, GKE Container API quota/outage, TLS/DNS/connectivity issues to remote endpoints (see `/Users/sjoerd/Documents/GitHub/agentregistry-inventory/internal/cluster/factory.go` and `/Users/sjoerd/Documents/GitHub/agentregistry-inventory/internal/cluster/gcp.go`); **Symptoms:** remote environments silently drop out or flap, inventory looks “randomly incomplete” across envs; **Detection:** controller errors “failed to create client for environment …”, stale `DiscoveryConfig.status.lastSyncTime`, UI discovery map showing disconnected; **Mitigation:** pre-validate environment config, monitor/raise GCP quotas, prefer static endpoint+CA for critical clusters, and add retries with exponential backoff/circuit-breaking for remote client creation.\n- **Failure mode:** CRD/RBAC drift breaks reconcile and/or returns inconsistent views; **Trigger:** agentregistry CRDs missing/outdated, external runtime CRDs (`kagent.dev`, `kmcp`) missing/incompatible, or RBAC doesn’t allow `list/watch` in discovered namespaces; **Symptoms:** reconcile errors like “no matches for kind …” or “forbidden,” deployments never materialize, discovery yields empty catalogs; **Detection:** controller logs + Kubernetes events on CRs, and `kubectl api-resources` / `kubectl auth can-i` against the controller SA; **Mitigation:** pin compatible CRD/controller versions, add startup preflight checks, and keep chart RBAC aligned with the discovery targets you configure.\n- **Failure mode:** Management-plane auth boundary gaps lead to unauthorized writes (or confusing lockouts) and supply-chain injection; **Trigger: